{% extends is_pdf|default(false) ? 'admin/_main/pdf_layout.html.twig' : 'admin/_main/layout.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Vendor Bill: {{ bill.billNumber }} | Admin{% endblock %}

{#
    The vendor bill, printed (queue items 15 and 45; the owner's ruling on item 44 that "every doc
    has a pdf and print version, same button layouts").

    Laid out from `purchase_order_document.html.twig`, which was itself laid out from the invoice's:
    same pdf_layout, same slim header bar, same meta/address/lines/totals rhythm, same shared
    `_purchase_document_styles.html.twig`, same dompdf constraints. A third document look would have
    been a third thing to maintain.

    ## What a bill prints that a purchase order does not, and why

    A purchase order says what we ORDERED. A bill says what we OWE, so the two halves the PO
    document deliberately refuses are exactly the two this one needs:

      - **amount paid and balance due.** A payable exists the moment a vendor bills us, and the
        balance is what the whole document is about. The PO's own comment says the payable "belongs
        on the vendor bill" — this is that document;
      - **remit-to.** "Send the money here" is nonsense on paperwork we send a supplier and is the
        single most important line on a bill we are paying. It is the FROZEN snapshot taken when the
        bill was entered (#606), not a live read of the vendor, because a factor or a lockbox
        changing next year must not restate where last year's payment was sent.

    ## And what it must NOT claim to be

    This is OUR record of THEIR invoice. It is not sent to anybody: a bill has no counterparty-facing
    existence the way an invoice does — the vendor already has their own copy, which is the document
    this one was typed from. So there is no Send action and no email template, and the footer says
    what the sheet is for, so nobody mistakes a printout of it for a demand we issued.
#}

{% block admin_body %}
    {% if not is_pdf|default(false) %}
    <section class="panel compact-panel no-print" style="margin-bottom:0;">
        <div class="panel-title-row">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Vendor bill document</p>
                <h1>{{ bill.billNumber }}</h1>
            </div>
            <div class="panel-actions">
                <a class="button back-button" href="{{ path('admin_bundle_procurement_bill', {id: bill.id}) }}">Back</a>
                <a class="button" href="{{ path('admin_bundle_procurement_bill_print', {id: bill.id, pdf: 1}) }}">Download PDF</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="po-page-container">
        <div class="po-document">

            <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="background:#0f172a;border-collapse:collapse;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;">
                <tr>
                    <td width="65%" style="background:#0f172a;padding:7px 16px;vertical-align:middle;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;">
                        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;color:#ffffff;">{{ site_name() }}</span>
                    </td>
                    <td width="35%" style="background:#0f172a;padding:7px 16px;vertical-align:middle;text-align:right;font-size:16px;font-weight:bold;color:#ffffff;letter-spacing:-0.02em;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;">VENDOR BILL</td>
                </tr>
            </table>

            <div class="po-body">

                <table class="po-meta-table" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                    <tr>
                        <td class="po-meta-col">
                            <p><strong>Bill number:</strong> <span style="color:#408dfb;">{{ bill.billNumber }}</span></p>
                            {# Their number, which is the only thing that can answer "have we seen
                               this one before" — it is what the duplicate-payment guard reads. #}
                            <p><strong>Their invoice number:</strong> {{ bill.vendorInvoiceNo|default('-') }}</p>
                            <p><strong>Bill date:</strong> {{ bill.documentDate ?: '-' }}</p>
                            <p><strong>Due:</strong> {{ bill.dueDate ?: 'not stated — due immediately' }}</p>
                            <p><strong>Currency:</strong> {{ bill.currency }}</p>
                            <p><strong>Against purchase order:</strong> {{ bill.purchaseOrder ? bill.purchaseOrder.poNumber : 'none' }}</p>
                            {# Never hidden and never only in prose — the owner's standing ruling. #}
                            <p><strong>Status:</strong> {{ bill.status }}</p>
                        </td>
                        <td class="po-meta-col">
                            {% if app_setting('company_name', '') %}<p><strong>{{ app_setting('company_name', '') }}</strong></p>{% endif %}
                            {% if app_setting('company_address', '') %}<p>{{ app_setting('company_address', '') }}</p>{% endif %}
                            {% set _cityLine = [app_setting('company_city', ''), province_name(app_setting('company_country', ''), app_setting('company_state', ''))]|filter(v => v)|join(', ') %}
                            {% if _cityLine %}<p>{{ _cityLine }}</p>{% endif %}
                            {% if app_setting('company_postal_code', '') %}<p>{{ app_setting('company_postal_code', '') }}</p>{% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="po-meta-col" style="text-align:right;">
                            <p><strong>Our account with you:</strong> {{ bill.vendor.accountNumber|default('-') }}</p>
                            {# The province frozen onto this bill when it was entered (queue item 32),
                               which is what the SHARED tax calculators matched on. Printed because a
                               bill whose tax looks wrong is usually a bill entered against the wrong
                               building. #}
                            <p><strong>Tax province:</strong> {{ bill.taxProvince|default('none recorded') }}</p>
                            <p><strong>GST Number:</strong> {{ app_setting('company_gst_number', '') ?: '-' }}</p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

                <div class="po-section-title">Billed By / Received At / Remit To</div>
                <table class="po-addr-table" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                    <tr>
                        <td class="address-box">
                            <h3>Billed By (Vendor):</h3>
                            <p><strong>{{ bill.vendorName ?: bill.vendor.name }}</strong></p>
                            {% set _vendorAddress = bill.vendor.defaultAddress ? bill.vendor.defaultAddress.toSnapshot() : '' %}
                            {% for addressLine in _vendorAddress|split("\n") %}
                                {% if addressLine|trim %}<p>{{ addressLine }}</p>{% endif %}
                            {% endfor %}
                            {% if bill.vendor.phone %}<p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong>Phone:</strong> {{ bill.vendor.phone }}</p>{% endif %}
                            {% if bill.vendor.email %}<p><strong>Email:</strong> {{ bill.vendor.email }}</p>{% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="address-box">
                            <h3>Received At:</h3>
                            {% if bill.warehouse %}
                                <p><strong>{{ bill.warehouse.name }}</strong></p>
                                {% if bill.warehouse.addressSummary %}<p>{{ bill.warehouse.addressSummary }}</p>{% endif %}
                            {% else %}
                                <p>No receiving warehouse recorded.</p>
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="address-box">
                            <h3>Remit To:</h3>
                            {% if bill.remitToAddress %}
                                {% for addressLine in bill.remitToAddress|split("\n") %}
                                    {% if addressLine|trim %}<p>{{ addressLine }}</p>{% endif %}
                                {% endfor %}
                            {% else %}
                                <p>No remit-to recorded — pay to the vendor's address above.</p>
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

                <div class="po-section-title">Items Billed</div>
                <table class="po-table" style="width:100%;table-layout:fixed;">
                    {# Column order: Description, Our SKU, Their part no., Quantity, Unit cost, Tax,
                       Line total — quantity sits immediately left of Unit cost, matching the
                       detail screen's own Description/SKU/Part No./Qty/Unit Cost shape, not
                       bunched at the far left ahead of everything else (#full-parity follow-up). #}
                    <colgroup>
                        <col style="width:31%;">
                        <col style="width:13%;">
                        <col style="width:13%;">
                        <col style="width:9%;">
                        <col style="width:11%;">
                        <col style="width:11%;">
                        <col style="width:12%;">
                    </colgroup>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Description</th>
                            <th>Our SKU</th>
                            <th>Their part no.</th>
                            <th>Quantity</th>
                            <th style="text-align:right;">Unit cost</th>
                            <th style="text-align:right;">Tax</th>
                            <th style="text-align:right;">Line total</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        {% for line in bill.lines %}
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>{{ line.name }}</strong></td>
                                <td>{{ line.sku|default('-') }}</td>
                                <td>{{ line.vendorSku|default('-') }}</td>
                                <td>{{ line.quantity|qty }}</td>
                                <td style="text-align:right;">{{ line.unitCost|price }}</td>
                                {# Off this bill's OWN frozen tax_lines snapshot, keyed by position —
                                   the same two arrays the detail page and the entry form read, so
                                   the three cannot print three figures for one line. #}
                                <td style="text-align:right;">{{ perLineTax[loop.index0]|default(0)|amount }}</td>
                                <td style="text-align:right;">{{ line.subtotal|amount }}</td>
                            </tr>
                        {% else %}
                            <tr><td colspan="7" class="empty-table-cell"><strong>This bill has no lines.</strong></td></tr>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <table class="po-footer-table" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                    <tr>
                        <td class="footer-note">
                            {% if bill.notes %}
                                <p class="footer-note-block"><strong>Notes:</strong> {{ bill.notes }}</p>
                            {% endif %}
                            {% if bill.purchaseOrder %}
                                <p class="footer-note-block">
                                    Entered against purchase order <strong>{{ bill.purchaseOrder.poNumber }}</strong>.
                                    The three-way match on the bill's own screen is what says whether the two agree.
                                </p>
                            {% else %}
                                <p class="footer-note-block">
                                    <strong>No purchase order behind this bill.</strong> It matches against nothing, which
                                    is an exception worth a human's eye rather than an error.
                                </p>
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="footer-totals">
                            {# Every row is stored: charges out of `charge_lines`, tax rows out of
                               `tax_lines`, and BILL TOTAL is the sum recalculateTotals() wrote from
                               exactly these. Amount paid and balance are the two rows the purchase
                               order document refuses and this one exists for. #}
                            <table class="totals-inner" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                                <tr><td>Subtotal (goods):</td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ bill.subtotal|amount }}</strong></td></tr>
                                {% for charge in chargeRows %}
                                    <tr><td>{{ charge.label }}:</td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ charge.amount|amount }}</strong></td></tr>
                                {% endfor %}
                                {% for taxLine in taxRows %}
                                    <tr><td>{{ taxLine.label }}{% if taxLine.rate is not null %} {{ (taxLine.rate * 100)|round(3) }}%{% endif %}:</td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ taxLine.amount|amount }}</strong></td></tr>
                                {% endfor %}
                                <tr><td>Total tax:</td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ bill.tax|amount }}</strong></td></tr>
                                <tr class="grand-total-row"><td><strong>BILL TOTAL ({{ bill.currency }}):</strong></td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ bill.total|amount }}</strong></td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Amount paid:</td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ bill.amountPaid|amount }}</strong></td></tr>
                                <tr class="grand-total-row"><td><strong>BALANCE DUE ({{ bill.currency }}):</strong></td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>{{ bill.balance|amount }}</strong></td></tr>
                            </table>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

                <p class="po-global-footer-note">
                    This is our record of the vendor's own invoice, printed for the file and for approval.
                    It is not sent to the vendor — they issued the invoice this was typed from.
                </p>

            </div>{# /po-body #}
        </div>{# /po-document #}
    </div>

    {% include '@Procurement/_purchase_document_styles.html.twig' %}
{% endblock %}
